  "real_issue_review": {
    "decision": "equivalent",
    "explanation": "The source and target segments are semantically identical. The source uses a negative imperative ('Do not unplug') which is correctly mapped to the Spanish negative imperative ('No desenchufe'). The temporal condition regarding the status light ('while its status light is on') is accurately reflected in the Spanish translation ('mientras la luz de estado est\u00e9 encendida'), maintaining the same obligation and scope. The claim that the Spanish text permits unplugging is incorrect; 'No desenchufe' is a direct prohibition.",
